      "writtenOn": "2025-10-07T18:47:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that all `hash_testcases.py` does is uniquely name each trace file based on the file contents. These files are then uploaded to a GCS bucket. So, there isn\u0027t any actual merging of data that happens. Hashing/uploading everything all at once vs. in pieces after each task should not make a difference - at the end of the day, the same files should be in the same location.",
      "parentUuid": "94e28d38_b904b623",
      "revId": "1b5742e6c0242c1a5bc6286399ede7bb79878a84",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
